Hand written, applies after the generated rename. BUG-542: a second conversion into a non-empty
deploy/ directory produced a corrupt rootfs. otapulse-convert-package created the output image with
`dd ... count=0 seek=N`, which extends an existing file but never truncates it, and the partitions are
written with conv=sparse (OTAPULSE_SPARSE_IMAGE=y), which skips all-zero blocks. Every block of the
previous image that the new content leaves as a hole therefore survived into the new image. The fix
removes a leftover output image before it is created. The plain copy deploy/NAME.<fs> and the artifact
were already overwritten, so only the .img was affected.

